Original commit body from 0a3833057a99285bcc32f97ea5320844aaea024c:

The opt-in scip-python backend (WI-nanom) never indexed the repository
it was asked to analyse:

- invoke ran `scip-python index <project> ...` from a scratch cwd.
  scip-python 0.6.6 takes no positional project; it silently ignores
  one and indexes its cwd, so every run indexed the empty scratch dir
  ("Total Project Files 0"), exited 0 and returned a valid empty index.
  On dev the whole-repo self-map with the backend opted in was
  node-for-node identical to the plain map (61,431 / 244,545). Now
  `--cwd <project>`.
- Without `--project-version` the indexer reads the git revision and,
  outside a git checkout, crashes on the first module
  (normalizeNameOrVersion). The recorded fixtures were produced with
  `--project-version 0.1.0`, which is why they worked. Now a constant
  "0": translation keys on descriptors only.
- The empty index read `no_candidate_construct`, a ROUTINE silence the
  [passes] line counts but never names. An empty index of a tree with
  Python in it is now `unreported`.
- A node heap exhaustion (V8's ~4 GB default; the whole hypergumbo tree
  aborted at 4.2 GB and indexed 1,712 files in 306 s at 8.4 GB with
  --max-old-space-size=9000) names NODE_OPTIONS in the failure message.

Evidence (real binary, 0.6.6): a 3-function non-git project opted in
-- dev: scip_python 0 nodes, no_candidate_construct; branch: 5 nodes,
5 edges, and `total -> Square.area` carries origin [python, scip].

